193:This paper is organized as follows. In Section 2, we study the computational complexity of the decision version of the internally-disjoint pendant Steiner tree packing problem in digraphs. When both $k\geq 3$, $\ell\geq 2$ are fixed integers, we prove that the problem of deciding whether there are at least $\ell$ pairwise internally-disjoint pendant $(S,r)$-trees in Eulerian digraphs is NP-complete, where $r\in S\subseteq V(D)$ and $|S|=k$ (Theorem \ref{thm2.2}). And this result implies the following Table~\ref{tab:Eulerian_digraphs}.
204:    $\ell \geq 2$ constant & NP-complete & NP-complete\\
